Subject: illumos: use the direct-assignment sigmask fallback (no glibc sigorset)

illumos declares sigorset() with the kernel k_sigset_t signature, not the glibc
three-argument sigset_t form the _POSIX_C_SOURCE branch assumes. Exclude __sun
from that branch so setChildSignalMask() uses the portable direct-assignment
fallback instead.

--- a/src/libutil/unix/signals.cc
+++ b/src/libutil/unix/signals.cc
@@ -105,7 +105,10 @@
 {
     assert(sigs); // C style function, but think of sigs as a reference
 
-#if _POSIX_C_SOURCE >= 1 || _XOPEN_SOURCE || _POSIX_SOURCE
+// illumos declares sigorset() with the kernel k_sigset_t signature, not the
+// glibc three-argument sigset_t form this branch assumes; exclude __sun so the
+// direct-assignment fallback below is used instead.
+#if (_POSIX_C_SOURCE >= 1 || _XOPEN_SOURCE || _POSIX_SOURCE) && !defined(__sun)
     sigemptyset(&savedSignalMask);
     // There's no "assign" or "copy" function, so we rely on (math) idempotence
     // of the or operator: a or a = a.
